descriptions.Refined Prototyping:
For personal-scale Open Artifice prototypes:
construction time is typically halved;
before committing rare materials, you may make one design analysis check to identify one major foreseeable flaw/missing property;
when substituting a material with matching required properties, reduce substitution penalty/difficulty by one step;
rebuilding a prototype you have already successfully built uses half ordinary consumable mundane material cost unless rare component was destroyed.

descriptions.Rage:
As a Bonus Action, enter Rage if not wearing heavy armour. It lasts 10 minutes and ends early if you are incapacitated or choose to end it as a Bonus Action. You can maintain it through the full duration as long as since the end of your previous turn you have done at least one of: made an attack roll, forced a creature to make a saving throw, taken damage, or used a Bonus Action to sustain the Rage.
While raging:
advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws;
resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage;
when you hit with a Strength-based weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, add +2 damage at levels 1–8, +3 at 9–15, +4 at 16–20;
you cannot cast spells or maintain concentration.
Rage uses are shown in the class table. Level 20 removes the limit. Recovery follows Terravale's external class-resource cadence.

descriptions.Wild Shape:
As a Bonus Action, expend one Wild Shape use to transform into a Beast or approved natural Aetherfauna form you have personally observed/studied. You do not use a fixed Known Forms list.
Uses: 2 per recovery cycle; at level 17, 3. Archdruid makes uses unlimited at 20. Maximum form CR: 1/4 at level 2, 1/2 at 4, 1 at 8, unless Circle of Moon improves it. No flying Speed before level 8; no swim Speed before level 4 unless race already has it or form is a special DM-approved exception.
On transformation:
retain Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma, alignment/personality, proficiencies, and class features that anatomy permits;
use form Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, AC, movement, senses, attacks;
gain temporary HP equal to Druid level + form's Constitution modifier + form CR×5 (minimum Druid level) rather than replacing your HP pool;
when temp HP are gone you remain transformed until duration ends, but further damage affects your normal HP;
duration = Druid level hours, or until dismissed as Bonus Action/incapacitated;
equipment merges, drops, or is worn if anatomy permits, chosen when transforming.
The DM may adjust a creature's stat block into a balanced Wild Shape profile; seeing a legendary/unique creature does not automatically grant legendary actions, lair actions, spellcasting, soul traits, or setting authority.

descriptions.Martial Arts:
While unarmoured/unshielded and using Unarmed Strikes or eligible Monk weapons:
use Dexterity instead of Strength for attack/damage;
replace weapon/Unarmed damage die with Martial Arts die if larger;
after taking Attack action, make one Unarmed Strike as Bonus Action.
Martial Arts die: d6 levels 1–4, d8 5–10, d10 11–16, d12 17–20. Monk weapons are simple melee weapons and martial melee weapons lacking Heavy/Special and with which a feature grants proficiency; Kensei can broaden this.

descriptions.Innate Sorcery:
Bonus Action, 2 uses per recovery cycle, enter heightened state for 1 minute. While active:
Sorcerer spell save DC +1;
advantage on attack rolls of Sorcerer spells;
visible/sensory manifestation may reflect Origin.
At level 7, Sorcery Incarnate improves this.
